          %h2#references References
          %h3#general General
          %p Original articles:
          %ul
            %li#Quillen68
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Quillen"}> Daniel Quillen
              ,
              %em
                The geometric realization of a Kan fibration is a Serre fibration. Proc. Amer. Math. Soc. 19 1968 1499–1500.
                %a{:href => "https://www.ams.org/journals/proc/1968-019-06/S0002-9939-1968-0238322-1/S0002-9939-1968-0238322-1.pdf"} pdf
          %p Monographs:
          %ul
            %li#GoerssJardine09
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Goerss"}> Paul Goerss
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J.+F.+Jardine"} J. F. Jardine
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Simplicial+homotopy+theory"} Simplicial homotopy theory
              %p
                Modern Birkh&amp;lbrack;er Classics (2009) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-3-0346-0189-4"}> doi:10.1007/978-3-0346-0189-4
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li#FP90
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rudolf+Fritsch"}> Rudolf Fritsch
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Renzo+A.+Piccinini"} Renzo A. Piccinini
                §4.2 and §4.3 in:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Cellular structures in topology
                %strong 19
                Cambridge University Press (1990) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9780511983948"}> doi:10.1017/CBO9780511983948
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://epub.ub.uni-muenchen.de/4493/1/4493.pdf"} pdf
          %p Lecture notes:
          %ul
            %li#Lackenby08
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marc+Lackenby"}> Marc Lackenby
              , Section I.2 of:
              %em Topology and Groups
